18. PROPS VS. STATE
================================================================================

PROPS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Pass data/configuration between components

Owned By:
Parent component

Received By:
Child component

Child Behavior:
Read-only

Example:

<SearchBar
  searchTerm={searchTerm}
/>


Inside Child:

function SearchBar({ searchTerm }) {
  ...
}


STATE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Purpose:
Store changing component/application data

Created With:

useState()

Example:

const [searchTerm, setSearchTerm] =
  useState('javascript');


Updated With:

setSearchTerm('react');


Simple Rule:

STATE
-> Component owns the data

PROPS
-> Component receives the data


